AUTO SIGNIN:
1. Enable Systemd Autologin on TTY1

Create a systemd drop-in configuration for getty@tty1:
```bash
sudo mkdir -p /etc/systemd/system/getty@tty1.service.d/
sudo nvim /etc/systemd/system/getty@tty1.service.d/override.conf
```
Paste the following content:
```toml
[Service]
ExecStart=
ExecStart=-/sbin/agetty --autologin nicolaivds --noclear %I $TERM
```

2. Auto-start Hyprland in .zprofile

Open or create ~/.zprofile (or ~/.zlogin):
`nvim ~/.zprofile`

Add this conditional block at the bottom:
```bash
if [ -z "$DISPLAY" ] && [ "$(tty)" = "/dev/tty1" ]; then
    echo -n "Starting Hyprland in 2s... (press ANY key / DEL to cancel)"

    if read -q -t 2 "?"; then
        echo -e "\nBypassed Hyprland. Dropping to standard shell."
    else
        echo -e "\nLaunching Hyprland..."
        exec Hyprland
    fi
fi
```